// =============================================================================
// SMART TREND PRO ENGINE
// =============================================================================
// This file contains SOURCE CODE ONLY.
// No rules, no version history, no design discussion, no architecture debate.
// Governing documents:
//   - Smart Trend Pro Engine Specification   (frozen architecture, PRIN-* rules)
//   - Smart Trend Pro Engine Development Log (history, freezes, amendments)
//
// Module Architecture below is FROZEN (Specification Section 4).
// New functionality is added INSIDE existing modules only (PRIN-MODULE-CONTAINMENT).
// New modules require the Architecture Amendment Procedure (Specification Section 10).
// =============================================================================

//@version=6

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FROZEN strategy() DECLARATION BLOCK
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// This block is part of the frozen architecture. Parameter values may be
// tuned; the presence/structure of this declaration is not to be altered
// outside the Architecture Amendment Procedure.
strategy(
     title                = "Smart Trend Pro Engine",
     shorttitle           = "STPE",
     overlay              = true,
     initial_capital      = 10000,
     default_qty_type     = strategy.percent_of_equity,
     default_qty_value    = 100,
     commission_type      = strategy.commission.percent,
     commission_value     = 0.0,
     slippage             = 0,
     calc_on_every_tick   = false,
     process_orders_on_close = true)


// #############################################################################
// LAYER ARCHITECTURE (frozen — Specification Section 3)
//
//   CORE LAYER
//       |
//   DATA LAYER
//       |
//   DECISION LAYER
//       |
//   SIGNAL LAYER
//       |
//   EXECUTION LAYER
//       |
//   INTERFACE LAYER
//       |
//   FUTURE LAYER
//
// Data flows strictly downward (PRIN-DATA-FLOW). A layer consumes only the
// immediately preceding layer's output (PRIN-LAYER-ISOLATION).
// #############################################################################


